+## Graph insights, part 1: clean topics and `kb context`
+
+## Why
+
+The explorer finds clusters, but topics are full of noise words (number, evening, goal, say) and plurals are split. This part cleans the topics and adds `kb context`, an offline command that prints a short Markdown block of past context from `graph.json`, so a future assistant does not need whole transcripts. Part 2 (analysis, insights, 2D map) is planned separately in `changes/2026-11-01-graph-map/`.
+
+## What changed
+
+| Phase | Title | Size | Review rounds | Bugs found and fixed |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 08 | Clean topics | medium | 2 | 1 |
+| 09 | `kb context` - token-light context for assistants (GraphRAG) | medium | 2 | 1 |
+
+2 of 2 phases done, one commit per phase.
+
+- `kb ingest` now writes cleaner topics: more stop words, plurals merged, technology terms preferred, generic words (in over 40% of sessions) dropped. The old topic functions are unchanged.
+- `kb context <words> [--out] [--limit] [--max-chars]` prints the best-matching sessions and their related topics, files and projects (4,000 characters by default). Exit codes: 0 (including no match), 1 (graph.json missing or unreadable), 2 (usage).
+
+## Risk and approvals
+
+High: it reads private conversation data and changes what the knowledge base writes. Everything stays on this computer; nothing is sent anywhere. **2 approvals needed.**
+
+## How to run the checks
+
+```bash
+cd core && cargo test && cargo clippy -- -D warnings
+cd ../explorer && npx vitest run
+```
+
+Try it:
+
+```bash
+kb ingest
+kb context "proposal app"
+```
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Tests and specs are locked, so no test covers `kubernetes` / `postgres` (they are kept unnormalised in topics and matched in `kb context`).
+- `kb context --max-chars` below 14 prints only the 14-character truncation marker.
+
+## More
+
+- Report: `changes/2026-11-01-graph-insights/report.md`
+- Article: `changes/2026-11-01-graph-insights/kba/kba.docx`
+- Undo: revert the two phase commits and re-run `kb ingest`.
